      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Elma Historical Society, founded in 1986, preserves the town’s past in a museum housed in the historic Elma Town Hall.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        10,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/21658",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Every year the society sponsors a scholarship for a local high school student who plans to study history in college.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/21658",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Elma sits in central Erie County, southeast of Buffalo, and is part of the Buffalo‑Niagara Falls metropolitan area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
